name: Direct lockfile scopes retain separate identities and unknown advisory policy
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_cargo_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/first-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_cargo_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART first
require-live-snap: 30 cargo-audit: 1 advisory findings | selected-a
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | first-identity
expect: a/Cargo.lock
submit: decision deferred Owned dependency declaration needs owner review
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_cargo_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART deferred
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 25 open generation: | initial-reference
expect: Reopen this observation
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 inspected file | selected-report
expect: Displayed Scan: completed
expect: a/Cargo.lock
expect: a/Cargo.lock · 1
expect: Advisory policy was not recorded
ask: Does Report keep the selected lockfile and unknown advisory policy visible even though the finite job completed?
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/second-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_cargo_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART second
paste-file: @ART/scope-compare.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 1 not reassessed | second-scope
expect: 0 not observed
keys: Escape
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/omitted-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_cargo_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART omitted
paste-file: @ART/policy-compare.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 1 not reassessed | changed-database-policy
expect: 0 not observed
expect: finding rule coverage was not recorded
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
resize: 160x48
live-snap: comparison-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: comparison-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: comparison-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: comparison-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: comparison-40x12
expect: 1 not reassessed
ask: Across six sizes, does the changed-database comparison avoid suggesting a fix when the advisory policy is unknown and target lockfiles are unchanged?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
paste-file: @ART/original-open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | original-decision
expect: a/Cargo.lock
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 25 open generation: | original-reference
expect: Reopen this observation
expect: This reference belongs to this workspace.
expect: List aliases can change as
expect: findings arrive.
ask: After F-0001 changes to another finding, is the displayed command a clear way to reopen this exact observation within its workspace?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/original-open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | restarted-review
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 25 open generation: | restarted-reference
expect: Reopen this observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_cargo_coverage.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain two separate lockfile findings, three installed offline audit outcomes and the original deferral with zero model requests or target execution?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
